# Rewrites, not redirects (status 200): the URL stays exactly where a
# visitor put it, only the served bytes change. One application behind
# all three routes - see page.js's own routing doc - so each of these
# just serves the same index.html, which then reads location.pathname
# itself to decide which of the three it is. spike/serve.py's own
# RewritingHandler does the same thing for local preview, since this
# file only has an effect on Cloudflare Pages.
/demo       /index.html   200
/originate  /index.html   200
/receive    /index.html   200
